From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 01:35:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 022/190] segacd: report the PCM chip's own address counter, so
 ears are optional

Still silent on hardware with every register field verified against
MAME and the emulated channel demonstrably running. The remaining
question -- driver or audio path -- cannot be settled from secondhand
cabling guides, which say the CD unit's audio does not cross the
expansion connector, while the JP BIOS boot music is pure RF5C164 and
hearing it would prove exactly the opposite.

So the VBL now samples channel 0's address counter while a note is
sounding and keeps the furthest value reached. It moves only if the
chip is genuinely playing. Reported in the spare bits of the drive
status word alongside the keyclick count.
---
 bios/segacd.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bios/segacd.c b/bios/segacd.c
index 22fca2a..f7c058a 100644
--- a/bios/segacd.c
+++ b/bios/segacd.c
@@ -123,6 +123,7 @@ static void pcm_reg(volatile UBYTE *reg, UBYTE v)
 
 static UBYTE pcm_countdown;             /* VBLs left before we silence it */
 static UBYTE pcm_clicks;                /* keyclicks actually requested */
+static UBYTE pcm_seen;                  /* furthest the channel ever got */
 static UBYTE pcm_ready;                 /* segacd_sound_init() completed */
 static UWORD bram_status;               /* base value of the status word */
 
@@ -269,7 +270,18 @@ void segacd_int_2_c(void)
     *(volatile UWORD *)0xFF802A = (UWORD)(bram_status
         | (pcm_ready ? 0x20 : 0)
         | ((conterm & 1) ? 0x40 : 0)
-        | ((UWORD)pcm_clicks << 8));
+        | ((UWORD)(pcm_clicks & 0x0F) << 8)
+        | ((UWORD)(pcm_seen & 0x0F) << 12));
+
+    /* Watch the channel's own address counter while a note is sounding.
+     * It only moves if the chip is genuinely playing, so this is the
+     * one reading that separates "the driver is broken" from "the
+     * audio never reaches a speaker" without anyone having to listen. */
+    if (pcm_countdown) {
+        UBYTE hi = *(volatile UBYTE *)0xFF0023;   /* channel 0 addr high */
+        if (hi > pcm_seen)
+            pcm_seen = hi;
+    }
 
     if (pcm_countdown) {                /* silence the bell when it is due */
         if (--pcm_countdown == 0)
